"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1JYDZZ4MS1S0MF77\",\"title\":\"U.S. Agroforestry & Reforestation using Long-term Leases — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"UNDER VALIDATION\",\"BIOSPHERE\",\"U.S. Agroforestry & Reforestation using Long-term Leases\",\"Propagate\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2026\",\"Project code\",\"1R8P\",\"Crediting period\",\"27 Mar 2022 to 27 Mar 2062\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"1R8P\",\"approval\":\"\",\"protocol_current\":\"Reforestation v1.1\",\"protocol_baseline\":\"Reforestation v1.0\",\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 2 of 2\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"23 Jul 2025\",\"Public Comment Period Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"23 Jun 2025\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://propagateag.com\",\"t\":\"Propagate\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/reforestation/1.1\",\"t\":\"Reforestation v1.1\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/reforestation/1.0\",\"t\":\"Reforestation v1.0\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1JV57MBN81S09WQB\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/standard#validation-and-verification-process\",\"t\":\"Isometric Standard\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JV57MBN81S09WQB/prj_1JYDZZ4MS1S0MF77/pjd_1K378VKQS1S00CMV/public_comment_period_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JV57MBN81S09WQB/prj_1JYDZZ4MS1S0MF77/pjd_1JYE1XCK11S0Q7AQ/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"UNDER VALIDATION\\nBIOSPHERE\\nU.S. Agroforestry & Reforestation using Long-term Leases\\nPropagate\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2026\\nProject code\\n1R8P\\nCrediting period\\n27 Mar 2022 to 27 Mar 2062\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nReforestation v1.1\\nBaseline protocol version\\nReforestation v1.0\\nSummary\\n\\nThe project aims to implement agroforestry practices such as alley cropping—combined with cover crops, reduced tillage, and improved residue management—by planting trees in rows on farmlands producing corn, soybeans, hay, and other monoculture grains.\\n\\nMason, KY\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiosphere carbon dioxide removal (CDR) harnesses the natural capacity of terrestrial and near-coastal ecosystems to absorb and store carbon for extended periods. These pathways utilize the biological processes of forests, soils, wetlands, and other ecosystems to capture carbon dioxide from the atmosphere and sequester it in biomass, soil organic matter, and sediments. Approaches to biosphere CDR include Reforestation, Agroforestry, Improved Forest Management, Mangrove Restoration, Peatland Restoration, and Soil Carbon Enhancement. Biosphere pathways often provide many co-benefits around the protection and enhancement of biodiversity alongside sustainable development for local communities.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 22 Jul 2025\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2025\\nInitial documentation submission\\nCompleted 2025\\nAudit kick-off\\nCompleted 2026\\nSite visit\\nExpected 2026\\nIN PROGRESS\\nApproval date\\n\\nIsometric officially approves the project having reviewed the validation report produced by the VVB, documenting the activities, results, and conclusion of the audit. A full list of content requirements for the report can be found in the Isometric Standard.\\n\\nExpected 2026\\nInitial credit issuance\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n23 Jul 2025\\tPublic Comment Period Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n23 Jun 2025\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 2 of 2\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"